aws-autoscaling-pipeline

The word-frequency worker in app/ is based on the AWS sample
"aws-go-wordfreq-sample" (https://github.com/aws-samples/aws-go-wordfreq-sample),
Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates, licensed under the Apache
License 2.0 (see LICENSE). The starter version used here adds 10-20 s of
simulated processing per file.

Changes in this repository: Go modules and a Docker build; app/session.go so
the same binary can target a local AWS emulator via AWS_ENDPOINT_URL; the
local/ stack (Moto, scaling policy re-creation, load test, plotting); the
documentation and redacted screenshots of the AWS deployment.

Later changes to the worker (October 2026), all off by default so the binary
behaves as it did on AWS: an opt-in hardened mode (WORKER_HARDENED=1) that
receives a message only when a worker is free, finishes the job in hand on
SIGTERM, writes results with a conditional put on file name and ETag, and
leaves unparseable messages for a dead-letter queue; the SQS SentTimestamp
and receive count recorded with each result, for measurement; and opt-in
crash injection (WORKER_CRASH_EVERY) for failure testing.
